      <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#XlNote"/>
      <euvoc:startDate rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2012-09-01</euvoc:startDate>
      <dct:created rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2018-02-26</dct:created>
      <rdf:value xml:lang="en">SKOS – Simple Knowledge Organization System – is a W3C recommendation designed for representation of thesauri, classification schemes, taxonomies, subject-heading systems or any other type of structured controlled vocabulary. XML – Extensible Markup Language – is a markup language that defines a set of rules for encoding documents in a format that is both human-readable and machine-readable.</rdf:value>
      <dct:creator>Wikipedia</dct:creator>
      <euvoc:xlNote xml:lang="en">SKOS – Simple Knowledge Organization System – is a W3C recommendation designed for representation of thesauri, classification schemes, taxonomies, subject-heading systems or any other type of structured controlled vocabulary. XML – Extensible Markup Language – is a markup language that defines a set of rules for encoding documents in a format that is both human-readable and machine-readable.</euvoc:xlNote>
   </euvoc:XlNote>
