      <dct:created rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2015-04-21</dct:created>
      <rdf:value xml:lang="en">The XYZ file format is a chemical file format. There is no formal standard and several variations exist, but a typical XYZ format specifies the molecule geometry by giving the number of atoms with Cartesian coordinates that will be read on the first line, a comment on the second, and the lines of atomic coordinates in the following lines.</rdf:value>
      <dct:creator>Wikipedia</dct:creator>
      <euvoc:xlNote xml:lang="en">The XYZ file format is a chemical file format. There is no formal standard and several variations exist, but a typical XYZ format specifies the molecule geometry by giving the number of atoms with Cartesian coordinates that will be read on the first line, a comment on the second, and the lines of atomic coordinates in the following lines.</euvoc:xlNote>
   </euvoc:XlNote>
