   <euvoc:XlNote rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/eb13ab3f09d1d4a7cd8a6637f25298a7">
      <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#XlNote"/>
      <euvoc:startDate rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2000-01-01</euvoc:startDate>
      <dct:created rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2021-08-27</dct:created>
      <rdf:value xml:lang="en">A DGN file is a 2D/3D drawing created by various construction CAD software, such as MicroStation and Intergraph Interactive Graphics Design System. It may be saved in one of two formats, either the Intergraph Standard File Format (ISFF) or the newer V8 DGN standard. DGN files are typically used to save designs for construction projects for highways, bridges, and buildings.</rdf:value>
      <dct:creator>The File Information Database</dct:creator>
      <dct:source>https://fileinfo.com/extension/dgn</dct:source>
      <euvoc:xlNote xml:lang="en">A DGN file is a 2D/3D drawing created by various construction CAD software, such as MicroStation and Intergraph Interactive Graphics Design System. It may be saved in one of two formats, either the Intergraph Standard File Format (ISFF) or the newer V8 DGN standard. DGN files are typically used to save designs for construction projects for highways, bridges, and buildings.</euvoc:xlNote>
   </euvoc:XlNote>
