      <rdf:value xml:lang="en">RDF Binary using Apache Thrift (‘RDF Thrift’) is a binary format for RDF and RDF-related data. Binary formats are faster to process – they do not incur the parsing costs of text-base formats. RDF Thrift defines basic encoding for RDF terms, then builds data formats for RDF graphs, RDF datasets and for SPARQL result sets. This gives a basis for high-performance linked data systems.</rdf:value>
      <dct:creator>Apache Jena</dct:creator>
      <dct:source>https://jena.apache.org/documentation/io/rdf-binary.html</dct:source>
      <euvoc:xlNote xml:lang="en">RDF Binary using Apache Thrift (‘RDF Thrift’) is a binary format for RDF and RDF-related data. Binary formats are faster to process – they do not incur the parsing costs of text-base formats. RDF Thrift defines basic encoding for RDF terms, then builds data formats for RDF graphs, RDF datasets and for SPARQL result sets. This gives a basis for high-performance linked data systems.</euvoc:xlNote>
   </euvoc:XlNote>
