   <euvoc:XlNote rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/d8e74c667db35ccba32cd7e1547dd01a">
      <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#XlNote"/>
      <euvoc:startDate rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2012-09-01</euvoc:startDate>
      <dct:created rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2018-02-26</dct:created>
      <rdf:value xml:lang="en">SGML – Standard Generalized Markup Language – is a standard for defining generalized markup languages for documents. DTD – document type definition – is a set of markup declarations that define a document type for an SGML-family markup language (SGML, XML, HTML). It defines the legal building blocks of an XML document, the document structure with a list of legal elements and attributes.</rdf:value>
      <dct:creator>Wikipedia</dct:creator>
      <euvoc:xlNote xml:lang="en">SGML – Standard Generalized Markup Language – is a standard for defining generalized markup languages for documents. DTD – document type definition – is a set of markup declarations that define a document type for an SGML-family markup language (SGML, XML, HTML). It defines the legal building blocks of an XML document, the document structure with a list of legal elements and attributes.</euvoc:xlNote>
   </euvoc:XlNote>
